 "qc_policy": "ERA5 publishes no per-value quality flag: a reanalysis value is the model's analysis. Values are stored in g/kg (1000 x the archive's kg/kg) (the archive's kg/kg x 1000, so float16 keeps them in its normal range). A value outside [-1, 40] becomes NaN and is COUNTED (`out_of_bounds`), never clipped. Pressure levels below the ground hold ERA5's own extrapolation and are kept. A NaN in any source cell a target cell averages makes that cell NaN (`source_nan_pixels`).",
